# promise: #738
# Little Windows on two desktops, each opened by a link from another app (`cover`, as in the report). Closing the
# last one on this desktop goes back to the app in use here, as closing a single one does (#430). The one on the
# other desktop took the keyboard instead (#646's rule), and macOS switched to that desktop. A test copy can't make
# desktops, so littleOtherDesktop marks the first window as opened on another one.
budget rss=900 stalls50=40
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true, "defaultLinkDestination": {"littleWindow": {}}}
pace 0.5

cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=main
wait 2
cra://debug?activate=1
wait 1
cover
cra://debug?yieldTo=${COVER}
wait 1
cover link
cra://debug?externalURL=${PAGE}?n=one
wait 2
cra://debug?littleOtherDesktop=0
cra://debug?yieldTo=${COVER}
wait 1
cover link
cra://debug?externalURL=${PAGE}?n=two
wait 2
cra://debug?littleFocus=open
expect-log little focus open: active=1 key=little1 over=0 windows=2

cra://action/closeTab
wait 1.5
cra://debug?littleFocus=closed
expect-log little focus closed: active=0 key=none over=\S+ windows=1
